IMPORT `roc-core`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 61: SECURITIES AND FUTURES ACT -- CIVIL LIABILITY ACTIONS (7 rules): a person who suffered loss from a
-- contravention of Part XII of the Securities and Futures Act, or from leveraged foreign exchange trading,
-- sues the contravening person (sections 234, 236D, 236G, 236I), asks the Court for permission (sections 235
-- and 236J), or claims compensation after a conviction or civil penalty order (sections 236 and 236K).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  A MAYBE BOOLEAN answer is:
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (the FALSE-kind comment quotes them).
--   NOTHING     the text does not answer on these facts (the NOTHING-kind comment says why).
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- O 3 r 2(1) is a caveat on every answer: every requirement in the Rules is subject to the Court's
-- discretion to order otherwise in the interests of justice; it is not threaded as an input.
-- What follows non-compliance with a Rule is O 3 r 2(4), except where this Order says so itself (rule 3(8)).
--
-- BORROWED FACTS.  The Securities and Futures Act is not among the sources.  Its sections (232, 234 to 236K)
-- are named in the inputs and asked as facts; who is a "claimant" or a "contravening person" in each
-- proceeding is given by the Act (rule 1(1)), and the encoding reports only which section gives the meaning.
-- Other Orders this Order applies (Order 6 rules 11 to 14, Order 9, Order 15 rule 7) are in other parts.
--
-- TIME.  O 3 r 3(1) says the Interpretation Act does not apply to the calculation of time in these Rules.
-- Whether an act was in time is a comparison with an input `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
-- (seam S-T1: roc1's O 3 r 3 computes it, and the merged file wires it).  The return date of an application
-- is a seam too (S-S1 gives the day service is deemed effected; the return date is fixed by the Court).

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 61 -- Securities and Futures Act, civil liability actions`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- definitions and application of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The proceedings the Order speaks of, by the section of the Act under which each is brought.
DECLARE `o 61 r 1 proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 234`
    `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 235`
    `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236`
    `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236D`
    `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236G`
    `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236I`
    `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236J`
    `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236K`
    `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under another section`

-- src:7057 | 1. —(1) In this Order — “Act” means the Securities and Futures Act, and any reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act;
@ref O 61 r 1(1) "Act" (src:7057)
`o 61 r 1(1) the Act` MEANS "the Securities and Futures Act"

-- "any reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act".  The text carves out no reference that
-- names another Act expressly; it is silent on one.
-- src:7057 | 1. —(1) In this Order — “Act” means the Securities and Futures Act, and any reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act;
@ref O 61 r 1(1) (src:7057)
GIVEN `the reference is to a section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference names another Act expressly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 1(1) a reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the reference names another Act expressly`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Rule does not say what a reference does that names another Act
        IF `the reference is to a section`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any reference to a section" speaks only of a reference to a section

-- "claimant": the section that gives the meaning, by the proceeding.  The meaning itself is in the Act, which is not
-- among the sources.
-- src:7058 | “claimant” — ( a )
-- src:7059 | in relation to a proceeding under section 234, 235 or 236, has the meaning given by section 234(1);
-- src:7060 | ( b )
-- src:7061 | in relation to a proceeding under section 236D, has the meaning given by section 236D(1);
-- src:7062 | ( c )
-- src:7063 | in relation to a proceeding under section 236G, has the meaning given by section 236G(1);
-- src:7064 | ( d )
-- src:7065 | in relation to a proceeding under section 236I, has the meaning given by section 236I(1); and
-- src:7066 | ( e )
-- src:7067 | in relation to a proceeding under section 236K, has the meaning given by section 236K(3);
@ref O 61 r 1(1) "claimant" (src:7058-7067)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `o 61 r 1 proceeding`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`o 61 r 1(1) "claimant" the section that gives its meaning` MEANS
    CONSIDER proceeding
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 234` THEN JUST "section 234(1)"
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 235` THEN JUST "section 234(1)"
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236` THEN JUST "section 234(1)"
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236D` THEN JUST "section 236D(1)"
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236G` THEN JUST "section 236G(1)"
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236I` THEN JUST "section 236I(1)"
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236J` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): no limb of "claimant" speaks of a proceeding under section 236J; QC: NOTHING (a bare list of limbs) / other: JUST FALSE (the definition is the list); a STRING cannot carry JUST FALSE, so the other reading would need a yes/no twin
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236K` THEN JUST "section 236K(3)"
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under another section` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): no limb of "claimant" speaks of a proceeding under any other section


-- src:7068 | “contravening person” — ( a )
-- src:7069 | in relation to a proceeding under section 234, 235 or 236, has the meaning given by section 234(1);
-- src:7070 | ( b )
-- src:7071 | in relation to a proceeding under section 236D, has the meaning given by section 236B(1) or 236C(1), as the case may be;
-- src:7072 | ( c )
-- src:7073 | in relation to a proceeding under section 236G, has the meaning given by section 236E(1) or 236F(1), as the case may be;
-- src:7074 | ( d )
-- src:7075 | in relation to a proceeding under section 236I, has the meaning given by section 236H(1);
-- src:7076 | ( e )
-- src:7077 | in relation to a proceeding under section 236J, has the meaning given by section 236B(1), 236C(1), 236E(1), 236F(1) or 236H(1), as the case may be; and
-- src:7078 | ( f )
-- src:7079 | in relation to a proceeding under section 236K, has the meaning given by section 236B(1), 236C(1), 236E(1), 236F(1) or 236H(1), as the case may be;
@ref O 61 r 1(1) "contravening person" (src:7068-7079)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `o 61 r 1 proceeding`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`o 61 r 1(1) "contravening person" the section that gives its meaning` MEANS
    CONSIDER proceeding
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 234` THEN JUST "section 234(1)"
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 235` THEN JUST "section 234(1)"
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236` THEN JUST "section 234(1)"
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236D` THEN JUST "section 236B(1) or 236C(1), as the case may be"
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236G` THEN JUST "section 236E(1) or 236F(1), as the case may be"
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236I` THEN JUST "section 236H(1)"
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236J` THEN JUST "section 236B(1), 236C(1), 236E(1), 236F(1) or 236H(1), as the case may be"
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236K` THEN JUST "section 236B(1), 236C(1), 236E(1), 236F(1) or 236H(1), as the case may be"
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under another section` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): no limb of "contravening person" speaks of a proceeding under any other section; QC as for "claimant"


-- src:7080 | “defendant corporation” has the meaning given by section 236A;
@ref O 61 r 1(1) "defendant corporation" (src:7080)
`o 61 r 1(1) "defendant corporation" the section that gives its meaning` MEANS "section 236A"

-- src:7082 | “defendant partnership” has the meaning given by section 236A.
@ref O 61 r 1(1) "defendant partnership" (src:7082)
`o 61 r 1(1) "defendant partnership" the section that gives its meaning` MEANS "section 236A"

-- "defendant individual" means an individual liable to an order for a civil penalty under section 236H in respect
-- of a contravention of any provision of Part XII committed by a corporation, partnership, limited liability
-- partnership or unincorporated association.  A "means" definition, so a case outside it is JUST FALSE.
-- src:7081 | “defendant individual” means an individual liable to an order for a civil penalty under section 236H in respect of a contravention of any provision of Part XII of the Act committed by a corporation, partnership, limited liability partnership or unincorporated association;
@ref O 61 r 1(1) "defendant individual" (src:7081)
GIVEN `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is liable to an order for a civil penalty under section 236H` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is in respect of a contravention of a provision of Part XII of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contravention was committed by a corporation, partnership, limited liability partnership or unincorporated association` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 1(1) "defendant individual" the person is a defendant individual` MEANS
    IF    `the person is an individual`
      AND `the person is liable to an order for a civil penalty under section 236H`
      AND `the order is in respect of a contravention of a provision of Part XII of the Act`
      AND `the contravention was committed by a corporation, partnership, limited liability partnership or unincorporated association`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an individual liable to an order for a civil penalty under section 236H in respect of a contravention of any provision of Part XII of the Act committed by a corporation, partnership, limited liability partnership or unincorporated association"

-- Rule 1(2): the Rules apply to proceedings under the eight sections, "subject to the following Rules of this Order".
-- src:7083 | (2) These Rules apply to proceedings under sections 234, 235, 236, 236D, 236G, 236I, 236J and 236K, subject to the following Rules of this Order.
@ref O 61 r 1(2) (src:7083)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `o 61 r 1 proceeding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 1(2) these Rules apply to the proceeding` MEANS
    CONSIDER proceeding
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under another section` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "These Rules apply to proceedings under sections 234, 235, 236, 236D, 236G, 236I, 236J and 236K" names the proceedings it reaches and says nothing of others
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2 -- commencement of an action under section 234, 236D, 236G or 236I`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1): "An action under section 234, 236D, 236G or 236I must be commenced by originating claim."
-- src:7085 | 2. —(1) An action under section 234, 236D, 236G or 236I must be commenced by originating claim. (2) Every application for permission of the Court under section 235(1) or 236J(1) or (3) to commence an action under section 234, 236D, 236G or 236I (as the case may be) must be made by originating application, naming as the defendant in the originating application the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual, as the case may be.
@ref O 61 r 2(1) (src:7085)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `o 61 r 1 proceeding`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 2(1) the action is one that the Rule names` MEANS
    CONSIDER proceeding
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 234` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236D` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236G` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236I` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:7085 | 2. —(1) An action under section 234, 236D, 236G or 236I must be commenced by originating claim. (2) Every application for permission of the Court under section 235(1) or 236J(1) or (3) to commence an action under section 234, 236D, 236G or 236I (as the case may be) must be made by originating application, naming as the defendant in the originating application the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual, as the case may be.
@ref O 61 r 2(1) (src:7085)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `o 61 r 1 proceeding`
      document IS A `Document kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 2(1) the action is commenced as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`o 61 r 2(1) the action is one that the Rule names` proceeding)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 2(1) speaks of "An action under section 234, 236D, 236G or 236I"
        IF document EQUALS `Originating claim`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be commenced by originating claim"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4) says what the Court may do about non-compliance) / other: JUST FALSE

-- (2): the application for permission is by originating application naming the right defendant.
-- src:7085 | 2. —(1) An action under section 234, 236D, 236G or 236I must be commenced by originating claim. (2) Every application for permission of the Court under section 235(1) or 236J(1) or (3) to commence an action under section 234, 236D, 236G or 236I (as the case may be) must be made by originating application, naming as the defendant in the originating application the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual, as the case may be.
@ref O 61 r 2(2) (src:7085)
GIVEN `the application is for permission under section 235(1) or 236J(1) or (3) to commence an action under section 234, 236D, 236G or 236I` IS A BOOLEAN
      document IS A `Document kind`
      `the defendant named is the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual, as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 2(2) the application for permission is made as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the application is for permission under section 235(1) or 236J(1) or (3) to commence an action under section 234, 236D, 236G or 236I`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 2(2) speaks of "Every application for permission of the Court under section 235(1) or 236J(1) or (3) to commence an action"
        IF document EQUALS `Originating application` AND `the defendant named is the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual, as the case may be`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be made by originating application, naming as the defendant"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- (3) and (4) of rule 3 are the same sentence about the originating application under rule 3.
-- "Unless expressly modified in this Rule, Order 6, Rules 11 to 14, Order 9 and Order 15, Rule 7 apply to every
-- originating application under this Rule."  An application of another Order, so what those Orders say is in other parts (S-L1).
-- src:7086 | (3) Unless expressly modified in this Rule, Order 6, Rules 11 to 14, Order 9 and Order 15, Rule 7 apply to every originating application under this Rule.
@ref O 61 r 2(3) (src:7086)
GIVEN `the application is an originating application under rule 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      provision IS A STRING
      `rule 2 expressly modifies the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 2(3) the provision applies to the originating application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the application is an originating application under rule 2`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 2(3) speaks of "every originating application under this Rule"
        IF NOT (elem provision (LIST
            "Order 6 rule 11",
            "Order 6 rule 12",
            "Order 6 rule 13",
            "Order 6 rule 14",
            "Order 9",
            "Order 15 rule 7"))
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only "Order 6, Rules 11 to 14, Order 9 and Order 15, Rule 7" are named
        IF `rule 2 expressly modifies the provision`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless expressly modified in this Rule"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (4): the supporting affidavit.
DECLARE `o 61 r 2(4) affidavit` HAS
    `o 61 r 2(4)(a) sets out particulars of the securities, futures contract or contract or arrangement in connection with the leveraged foreign exchange trading transaction in question` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 61 r 2(4)(b) sets out the circumstances leading to the entering into of the transaction in question` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 61 r 2(4)(c) sets out the circumstances leading to the loss suffered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 61 r 2(4)(d) sets out particulars of the loss suffered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 61 r 2(4)(e) sets out the grounds on which the application is made` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:7087 | (4) The application under paragraph (2) must be supported by an affidavit setting out — ( a )
-- src:7088 | particulars of the securities, futures contract or contract or arrangement in connection with the leveraged foreign exchange trading transaction in question;
-- src:7089 | ( b )
-- src:7090 | circumstances leading to the entering into of the transaction in question;
-- src:7091 | ( c )
-- src:7092 | circumstances leading to the loss suffered;
-- src:7093 | ( d )
-- src:7094 | particulars of the loss suffered; and
-- src:7095 | ( e )
-- src:7096 | the grounds on which the application is made.
@ref O 61 r 2(4) (src:7087-7096)
GIVEN affidavit IS A `o 61 r 2(4) affidavit`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`o 61 r 2(4) the matters the affidavit has not yet set out` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (IF affidavit's `o 61 r 2(4)(a) sets out particulars of the securities, futures contract or contract or arrangement in connection with the leveraged foreign exchange trading transaction in question` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(a) particulars of the securities, futures contract or contract or arrangement in connection with the leveraged foreign exchange trading transaction in question"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 61 r 2(4)(b) sets out the circumstances leading to the entering into of the transaction in question` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(b) circumstances leading to the entering into of the transaction in question"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 61 r 2(4)(c) sets out the circumstances leading to the loss suffered` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(c) circumstances leading to the loss suffered"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 61 r 2(4)(d) sets out particulars of the loss suffered` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(d) particulars of the loss suffered"),
        (IF affidavit's `o 61 r 2(4)(e) sets out the grounds on which the application is made` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "(e) the grounds on which the application is made"))

-- src:7087 | (4) The application under paragraph (2) must be supported by an affidavit setting out — ( a )
-- src:7088 | particulars of the securities, futures contract or contract or arrangement in connection with the leveraged foreign exchange trading transaction in question;
-- src:7089 | ( b )
-- src:7090 | circumstances leading to the entering into of the transaction in question;
-- src:7091 | ( c )
-- src:7092 | circumstances leading to the loss suffered;
-- src:7093 | ( d )
-- src:7094 | particulars of the loss suffered; and
-- src:7095 | ( e )
-- src:7096 | the grounds on which the application is made.
@ref O 61 r 2(4) (src:7087-7096)
GIVEN affidavit IS A `o 61 r 2(4) affidavit`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 2(4) the affidavit supporting the application sets out what the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF count (`o 61 r 2(4) the matters the affidavit has not yet set out` affidavit) EQUALS 0
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be supported by an affidavit setting out"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- (5): service "in the first instance ... only on" the person named, unless the Court directs service on another.
-- A closed "only" list: service on anyone else without a direction is JUST FALSE; service on the named person is as required.
-- src:7097 | (5) The application under paragraph (2) and supporting affidavit under paragraph (4) must in the first instance be served only on the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual (as the case may be) but the Court may direct the application and supporting affidavit to be served on any other person appearing to be interested.
@ref O 61 r 2(5) (src:7097)
GIVEN `the application and affidavit are served on the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual, as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are served on any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has directed service on that other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 2(5) the application is served as the Rule requires in the first instance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `they are served on any other person` AND NOT (`the Court has directed service on that other person`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must in the first instance be served only on the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual (as the case may be)"
        IF `the application and affidavit are served on the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual, as the case may be`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): not yet served on the person the Rule names; a bare "must ... be served"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

