-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 3 -- application for directions on claims under section 236 or 236K`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1): who may apply.  "(other than by way of a default judgment or a consent order)" takes a civil penalty order made
-- by default or consent out of what a grant ("may apply") covers.  QE: NOTHING for X (the parenthesis limits a grant: it says what the permission does not cover and does not say that no one may apply) / other: JUST FALSE (read as "except": a civil penalty order made by default judgment or by consent cannot found an application under rule 3(1), so a claimant who relies only on one may not apply)
-- src:7101 | 3. —(1) A claimant seeking compensation from a contravening person referred to in section 234(1), defendant corporation, defendant partnership or defendant individual — ( a )
-- src:7102 | convicted for a contravention of any provision of Part XII of the Act; or
-- src:7103 | ( b )
-- src:7104 | against whom an order for a civil penalty is made under section 232, 236B, 236C, 236E, 236F or 236H (other than by way of a default judgment or a consent order),
-- src:7105 | as the case may be, may apply to the Court for directions on claims for compensation in respect of that contravention, and the Court may, subject to section 236(2) or to section 236K(2) read with section 236(2) (as the case may be) fix a return date for hearing the application.
@ref O 61 r 3(1) (src:7101-7105)
GIVEN `the claimant seeks compensation from the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was convicted for a contravention of a provision of Part XII of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a civil penalty order was made against the person under section 232, 236B, 236C, 236E, 236F or 236H` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that order was made by way of a default judgment or a consent order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 3(1) the claimant may apply for directions on claims for compensation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the claimant seeks compensation from the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 3(1) gives the permission to "A claimant seeking compensation from" those persons
        IF `the person was convicted for a contravention of a provision of Part XII of the Act`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `a civil penalty order was made against the person under section 232, 236B, 236C, 236E, 236F or 236H` AND NOT (`that order was made by way of a default judgment or a consent order`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `a civil penalty order was made against the person under section 232, 236B, 236C, 236E, 236F or 236H`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(other than by way of a default judgment or a consent order)" takes such an order out of what the permission covers and does not say that no one may apply; QE: NOTHING (the parenthesis limits the grant and does not say that no one may apply) / other: JUST FALSE (read as "except": an order made by default judgment or by consent cannot found an application under rule 3(1))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the permission names the two cases (a) and (b) and says nothing of any other

-- src:7105 | as the case may be, may apply to the Court for directions on claims for compensation in respect of that contravention, and the Court may, subject to section 236(2) or to section 236K(2) read with section 236(2) (as the case may be) fix a return date for hearing the application.
@ref O 61 r 3(1) (src:7105)
GIVEN `an application for directions has been made under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 236(2), or section 236K(2) read with section 236(2), permits the Court to fix a return date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 3(1) the Court may fix a return date for hearing the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`an application for directions has been made under paragraph (1)`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given for "hearing the application" made under paragraph (1)
        IF `section 236(2), or section 236K(2) read with section 236(2), permits the Court to fix a return date`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the power is "subject to section 236(2) or to section 236K(2) read with section 236(2)", which are in the Act

-- (2): "must not be made before the conviction or the order ... has been made final".  An "until" bar, its own yes/no
-- (ruling of 2026-11-05 (d)): JUST TRUE until it is final, JUST FALSE after.  Nothing here says the application MAY be made after.
-- src:7106 | (2) An application under paragraph (1) must not be made before the conviction or the order making the civil penalty has been made final in accordance with section 236(4) or (5) or with section 236K(2) read with section 236(4) or (5), as the case may be.
@ref O 61 r 3(2) (src:7106)
GIVEN `the application is one under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conviction or the order making the civil penalty has been made final in accordance with section 236(4) or (5) or with section 236K(2) read with section 236(4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 3(2) an application cannot yet be made because the conviction or order is not yet final` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the application is one under paragraph (1)`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application under paragraph (1)"
        IF NOT (`the conviction or the order making the civil penalty has been made final in accordance with section 236(4) or (5) or with section 236K(2) read with section 236(4) or (5)`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be made before the conviction or the order making the civil penalty has been made final"

-- The bar as a prohibition on a trace.  "An application under paragraph (1) must not be made": the person who makes it
-- is the claimant of paragraph (1), the only person who "may apply", so the claimant is the named bearer.
DECLARE `o 61 r 3(2) party` IS ONE OF
    `o 61 r 3(2) the claimant`

DECLARE `o 61 r 3(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `o 61 r 3(2) apply for directions on claims for compensation`

GIVEN `days until the conviction or order is made final` IS A NUMBER
`o 61 r 3(2) the prohibition on applying before the conviction or order is final` MEANS
    PARTY `o 61 r 3(2) the claimant`
    SHANT `o 61 r 3(2) apply for directions on claims for compensation`
    WITHIN `days until the conviction or order is made final`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 61 r 3(2) the claimant` BECAUSE "the application for directions was made before the conviction or order was final (O 61 r 3(2))"

#TRACE `o 61 r 3(2) the prohibition on applying before the conviction or order is final` 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 61 r 3(2) the claimant` DOES `o 61 r 3(2) apply for directions on claims for compensation` AT 4
#TRACE `o 61 r 3(2) the prohibition on applying before the conviction or order is final` 10 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 11

-- (3)
-- src:7107 | (3) Every application under paragraph (1) must be made by originating application.
@ref O 61 r 3(3) (src:7107)
GIVEN `the application is one under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      document IS A `Document kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 3(3) the application for directions is made as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the application is one under paragraph (1)`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 3(3) speaks of "Every application under paragraph (1)"
        IF document EQUALS `Originating application`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be made by originating application"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- (4): as rule 2(3), for an originating application under rule 3.
-- src:7108 | (4) Unless expressly modified in this Rule, Order 6, Rules 11 to 14, Order 9 and Order 15, Rule 7 apply to every originating application under this Rule.
@ref O 61 r 3(4) (src:7108)
GIVEN `the application is an originating application under rule 3` IS A BOOLEAN
      provision IS A STRING
      `rule 3 expressly modifies the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 3(4) the provision applies to the originating application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the application is an originating application under rule 3`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 3(4) speaks of "every originating application under this Rule"
        IF NOT (elem provision (LIST
            "Order 6 rule 11",
            "Order 6 rule 12",
            "Order 6 rule 13",
            "Order 6 rule 14",
            "Order 9",
            "Order 15 rule 7"))
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only "Order 6, Rules 11 to 14, Order 9 and Order 15, Rule 7" are named
        IF `rule 3 expressly modifies the provision`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless expressly modified in this Rule"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (5): "Unless the Court otherwise orders, the application must be served personally at least 28 clear days or such
-- longer time as the Court may direct before the return date, on the contravening person, ...".
-- src:7109 | (5) Unless the Court otherwise orders, the application must be served personally at least 28 clear days or such longer time as the Court may direct before the return date, on the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual, as the case may be.
@ref O 61 r 3(5) (src:7109)
`o 61 r 3(5) the period for serving the application before the return date` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 28
    `period unit` IS `Clear days`
    `period direction` IS `Before the anchor`

-- src:7109 | (5) Unless the Court otherwise orders, the application must be served personally at least 28 clear days or such longer time as the Court may direct before the return date, on the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual, as the case may be.
@ref O 61 r 3(5) (src:7109)
