    IF `the Court otherwise orders`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the Court otherwise orders"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- The last day for serving is the later of the 28th clear day before the return date and any longer time the Court
-- directed counted back from it (a made-up date in the tests; O 3 r 3 computes it).
-- src:7109 | (5) Unless the Court otherwise orders, the application must be served personally at least 28 clear days or such longer time as the Court may direct before the return date, on the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual, as the case may be.
@ref O 61 r 3(5) (src:7109)
GIVEN `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is served personally on the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual, as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date it was served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 3(5) the application is served as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Court otherwise orders`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty does not arise; QD: NOTHING, and the companion `o 61 r 3(5) the duty to serve the application personally in time arises` answers JUST FALSE / other: JUST TRUE (nothing is unmet)
        IF `the date it was served` GREATER THAN `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at least 28 clear days or such longer time as the Court may direct before the return date"
        IF `the application is served personally on the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual, as the case may be`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): not served personally on the person the Rule names; a bare "must be served personally"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4) and rule 3(8)) / other: JUST FALSE

-- A plain yes/no for rule 3(8): whether the claimant complied with paragraph (5).  A duty lifted by the Court is complied with.
GIVEN `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is served personally on the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual, as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date it was served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 3(5) the claimant complied with paragraph (5)` MEANS
    `the Court otherwise orders` OR (`o 61 r 3(5) the application is served as the Rule requires` `the Court otherwise orders` `the application is served personally on the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual, as the case may be` `the date it was served` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` EQUALS JUST TRUE)

-- (6): advertisement in Form 91, "at least 21 clear days or such longer time as the Court may direct before the return
