        IF `the advertisement is in Form 91` AND (`it appeared at least once in one English and one Chinese local daily newspaper` OR `the Court directed another newspaper and it appeared there`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be advertised in Form 91 ... at least once in one English and one Chinese local daily newspaper"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4) and rule 3(8)) / other: JUST FALSE

GIVEN `the advertisement is in Form 91` IS A BOOLEAN
