-- (7): what the advertisement states.  The solicitor's name and address are required where the applicant has a solicitor.
DECLARE `o 61 r 3(7) advertisement` HAS
    `o 61 r 3(7) states the day on which the application was filed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 61 r 3(7) states the name and address of the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 61 r 3(7) the applicant has a solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 61 r 3(7) states the name and address of the applicant's solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:7111 | (7) The advertisement must state the day on which the application was filed and the name and address of the applicant and of the applicant’s solicitor.
@ref O 61 r 3(7) (src:7111)
GIVEN advertisement IS A `o 61 r 3(7) advertisement`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`o 61 r 3(7) the matters the advertisement has not yet stated` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (IF advertisement's `o 61 r 3(7) states the day on which the application was filed` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "the day on which the application was filed"),
        (IF advertisement's `o 61 r 3(7) states the name and address of the applicant` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "the name and address of the applicant"),
        (IF (NOT (advertisement's `o 61 r 3(7) the applicant has a solicitor`)) OR advertisement's `o 61 r 3(7) states the name and address of the applicant's solicitor` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "the name and address of the applicant's solicitor"))

-- src:7111 | (7) The advertisement must state the day on which the application was filed and the name and address of the applicant and of the applicant’s solicitor.
@ref O 61 r 3(7) (src:7111)
GIVEN advertisement IS A `o 61 r 3(7) advertisement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 3(7) the advertisement states what the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF count (`o 61 r 3(7) the matters the advertisement has not yet stated` advertisement) EQUALS 0
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must state"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4) and rule 3(8)) / other: JUST FALSE

GIVEN advertisement IS A `o 61 r 3(7) advertisement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 3(7) the claimant complied with paragraph (7)` MEANS
    `o 61 r 3(7) the advertisement states what the Rule requires` advertisement EQUALS JUST TRUE

