-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 4 -- proof of claim under section 236 or 236K`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1): "At least 7 clear days before the return date ..., each claimant desiring to claim compensation ... must state the
-- claimant's claim by filing an affidavit".
-- src:7114 | 4. —(1) At least 7 clear days before the return date of the application under Rule 3(1), each claimant desiring to claim compensation against the contravening person referred to in section 234(1), the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual (as the case may be) (each called in this Rule the subject) under section 236 or 236K in respect of the same contravention for which the subject had been convicted or had a civil penalty order under section 232, 236B, 236C, 236E, 236F or 236H (as the case may be) made against the subject, must state the claimant’s claim by filing an affidavit in accordance with paragraph (2). (2) The affidavit must be supported by the relevant exhibits, and must explain the grounds on which the claimant’s claim is made, including — ( a )
@ref O 61 r 4(1) (src:7114)
`o 61 r 4(1) the period for filing the affidavit of claim before the return date` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 7
    `period unit` IS `Clear days`
    `period direction` IS `Before the anchor`

-- src:7114 | 4. —(1) At least 7 clear days before the return date of the application under Rule 3(1), each claimant desiring to claim compensation against the contravening person referred to in section 234(1), the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual (as the case may be) (each called in this Rule the subject) under section 236 or 236K in respect of the same contravention for which the subject had been convicted or had a civil penalty order under section 232, 236B, 236C, 236E, 236F or 236H (as the case may be) made against the subject, must state the claimant’s claim by filing an affidavit in accordance with paragraph (2). (2) The affidavit must be supported by the relevant exhibits, and must explain the grounds on which the claimant’s claim is made, including — ( a )
@ref O 61 r 4(1) (src:7114)
GIVEN `the claimant desires to claim compensation against the subject under section 236 or 236K in respect of the same contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 4(1) the duty to file an affidavit of claim arises` MEANS
    IF `the claimant desires to claim compensation against the subject under section 236 or 236K in respect of the same contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "each claimant desiring to claim compensation against the contravening person"

-- src:7114 | 4. —(1) At least 7 clear days before the return date of the application under Rule 3(1), each claimant desiring to claim compensation against the contravening person referred to in section 234(1), the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual (as the case may be) (each called in this Rule the subject) under section 236 or 236K in respect of the same contravention for which the subject had been convicted or had a civil penalty order under section 232, 236B, 236C, 236E, 236F or 236H (as the case may be) made against the subject, must state the claimant’s claim by filing an affidavit in accordance with paragraph (2). (2) The affidavit must be supported by the relevant exhibits, and must explain the grounds on which the claimant’s claim is made, including — ( a )
@ref O 61 r 4(1) (src:7114)
GIVEN `the claimant desires to claim compensation against the subject under section 236 or 236K in respect of the same contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the affidavit was filed, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date being asked about` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 4(1) the claimant files the affidavit of claim in time` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the claimant desires to claim compensation against the subject under section 236 or 236K in respect of the same contravention`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty does not arise; QD: NOTHING, and the companion `o 61 r 4(1) the duty to file an affidavit of claim arises` answers JUST FALSE / other: JUST TRUE (nothing is unmet)
    ELSE CONSIDER `the date the affidavit was filed, if it was`
        WHEN JUST filed THEN
            IF filed AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "At least 7 clear days before the return date of the application"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            IF `the date being asked about` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no affidavit is filed yet and the time for filing it has not yet run out
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "At least 7 clear days before the return date of the application"

-- (2): the affidavit "must be supported by the relevant exhibits, and must explain the grounds ... including" (a) to (d).
DECLARE `o 61 r 4(2) affidavit` HAS
    `o 61 r 4(2) is supported by the relevant exhibits` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 61 r 4(2) explains the grounds on which the claim is made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 61 r 4(2)(a) includes particulars of the securities, futures contract or contract or arrangement in connection with the leveraged foreign exchange trading transaction in question` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 61 r 4(2)(b) includes the circumstances leading to the entering into of the transaction in question` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 61 r 4(2)(c) includes the circumstances leading to the loss suffered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 61 r 4(2)(d) includes particulars of the loss suffered` IS A BOOLEAN

