-- (3): "the exhibits may include" (a) trade notes or slips, (b) statements of accounts for the relevant period,
-- (c) copies of instructions given to a broker or remisier.  "Without limiting paragraph (2)": the list is not closed.
DECLARE `o 61 r 4(3) exhibit` IS ONE OF
    `o 61 r 4(3)(a) trade notes or slips`
    `o 61 r 4(3)(b) statements of accounts for the relevant period`
    `o 61 r 4(3)(c) copies of instructions given to a broker or remisier`
    `o 61 r 4(3) another exhibit`

-- src:7122 | (3) Without limiting paragraph (2), the exhibits may include — ( a )
-- src:7123 | trade notes or slips;
-- src:7124 | ( b )
-- src:7125 | statements of accounts for the relevant period; and
-- src:7126 | ( c )
-- src:7127 | copies of instructions given to a broker or remisier.
@ref O 61 r 4(3) (src:7122-7127)
GIVEN exhibit IS A `o 61 r 4(3) exhibit`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 4(3) the exhibits may include` MEANS
    CONSIDER exhibit
    WHEN `o 61 r 4(3) another exhibit` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Without limiting paragraph (2), the exhibits may include" names three and does not close the list
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (4): "Every claimant must serve on the subject a copy of the affidavit within 3 days of the filing of the same."
-- src:7128 | (4) Every claimant must serve on the subject a copy of the affidavit within 3 days of the filing of the same.
@ref O 61 r 4(4) (src:7128)
`o 61 r 4(4) the period for serving a copy of the affidavit on the subject` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 3
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:7128 | (4) Every claimant must serve on the subject a copy of the affidavit within 3 days of the filing of the same.
@ref O 61 r 4(4) (src:7128)
GIVEN `the date a copy was served on the subject, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date being asked about` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 4(4) the claimant serves a copy of the affidavit on the subject in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date a copy was served on the subject, if it was`
    WHEN JUST served THEN
        IF served AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 3 days of the filing of the same"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the date being asked about` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no copy is served yet and the time for serving it has not yet run out
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 3 days of the filing of the same"

DECLARE `o 61 r 4(4) party` IS ONE OF
    `o 61 r 4(4) the claimant`

DECLARE `o 61 r 4(4) act` IS ONE OF
    `o 61 r 4(4) serve a copy of the affidavit on the subject`

-- The trace's time unit is a day counted from the filing of the affidavit, as O 3 r 3 counts days.
`o 61 r 4(4) the duty to serve a copy of the affidavit` MEANS
    PARTY `o 61 r 4(4) the claimant`
    MUST `o 61 r 4(4) serve a copy of the affidavit on the subject`
    WITHIN 3
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 61 r 4(4) the claimant` BECAUSE "a copy of the affidavit was not served on the subject within 3 days of its filing (O 61 r 4(4))"

#TRACE `o 61 r 4(4) the duty to serve a copy of the affidavit` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 61 r 4(4) the claimant` DOES `o 61 r 4(4) serve a copy of the affidavit on the subject` AT 3
#TRACE `o 61 r 4(4) the duty to serve a copy of the affidavit` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 4

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 5 -- powers of the Court hearing the application`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 61 r 5(1) kind of direction or order` IS ONE OF
    `o 61 r 5(1)(a) for the filing of such further affidavit as the Court considers necessary`
    `o 61 r 5(1)(b) on the manner in which proceedings are to be instituted by the claimants against the defendant`
    `o 61 r 5(1)(c) that an issue between the claimants and the defendant be stated and tried`
    `o 61 r 5(1)(d) that the matter be adjourned`
    `o 61 r 5(1)(e) that further advertisements be made in addition to that required under Rule 3(6)`
    `o 61 r 5(1)(f) for the substitution of the claimant making the application with another claimant`
    `o 61 r 5(1)(g) that the application be dismissed`
    `o 61 r 5(1) another kind of direction or order`

-- "where, on the hearing of an application made under Rule 3(1), all the persons on whom the application has been
-- served and all claimants who have filed their affidavits of claim appear, the Court may give such directions or
-- make such orders ... as the Court thinks best adapted to secure the just, expeditious and economical disposal of
-- the proceedings, including directions or orders" (a) to (g).
-- src:7130 | 5. —(1) Without limiting Order 6, Rules 11 to 14, Order 9 and Order 15, Rule 7, where, on the hearing of an application made under Rule 3(1), all the persons on whom the application has been served and all claimants who have filed their affidavits of claim appear, the Court may give such directions or make such orders as to the further conduct of the proceedings as the Court thinks best adapted to secure the just, expeditious and economical disposal of the proceedings, including directions or orders — ( a )
-- src:7131 | for the filing of such further affidavit as the Court considers necessary;
-- src:7132 | ( b )
-- src:7133 | on the manner in which proceedings are to be instituted by the claimants against the defendant;
-- src:7134 | ( c )
-- src:7135 | that an issue between the claimants and the defendant be stated and tried;
-- src:7136 | ( d )
-- src:7137 | that the matter be adjourned;
-- src:7138 | ( e )
-- src:7139 | that further advertisements be made in addition to that required under Rule 3(6) in the manner required by the Court;
-- src:7140 | ( f )
-- src:7141 | for the substitution of the claimant making the application with another claimant; or
-- src:7142 | ( g )
-- src:7143 | that the application be dismissed.
@ref O 61 r 5(1) (src:7130-7143)
GIVEN `the Court is hearing an application made under Rule 3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the persons on whom the application has been served appear` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all claimants who have filed their affidavits of claim appear` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 5(1) the Court may give directions or make orders on the hearing` MEANS
    IF `the Court is hearing an application made under Rule 3(1)` AND `all the persons on whom the application has been served appear` AND `all claimants who have filed their affidavits of claim appear`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where, on the hearing of an application made under Rule 3(1), all the persons on whom the application has been served and all claimants who have filed their affidavits of claim appear"

-- src:7130 | 5. —(1) Without limiting Order 6, Rules 11 to 14, Order 9 and Order 15, Rule 7, where, on the hearing of an application made under Rule 3(1), all the persons on whom the application has been served and all claimants who have filed their affidavits of claim appear, the Court may give such directions or make such orders as to the further conduct of the proceedings as the Court thinks best adapted to secure the just, expeditious and economical disposal of the proceedings, including directions or orders — ( a )
-- src:7131 | for the filing of such further affidavit as the Court considers necessary;
-- src:7132 | ( b )
-- src:7133 | on the manner in which proceedings are to be instituted by the claimants against the defendant;
-- src:7134 | ( c )
-- src:7135 | that an issue between the claimants and the defendant be stated and tried;
-- src:7136 | ( d )
-- src:7137 | that the matter be adjourned;
-- src:7138 | ( e )
-- src:7139 | that further advertisements be made in addition to that required under Rule 3(6) in the manner required by the Court;
-- src:7140 | ( f )
-- src:7141 | for the substitution of the claimant making the application with another claimant; or
-- src:7142 | ( g )
-- src:7143 | that the application be dismissed.
@ref O 61 r 5(1) (src:7130-7143)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 61 r 5(1) kind of direction or order`
      `the Court is hearing an application made under Rule 3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the persons on whom the application has been served appear` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all claimants who have filed their affidavits of claim appear` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court thinks it best adapted to secure the just, expeditious and economical disposal of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 5(1) the Court may give this kind of direction or make this kind of order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`o 61 r 5(1) the Court may give directions or make orders on the hearing` `the Court is hearing an application made under Rule 3(1)` `all the persons on whom the application has been served appear` `all claimants who have filed their affidavits of claim appear` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where, on the hearing of an application made under Rule 3(1), all the persons on whom the application has been served and all claimants who have filed their affidavits of claim appear"
        IF kind EQUALS `o 61 r 5(1) another kind of direction or order`
        THEN (IF `the Court thinks it best adapted to secure the just, expeditious and economical disposal of the proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "including" does not close the list, and an unlisted kind is within the power only if the Court thinks it best adapted
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:7144 | (2) Where a contravening person, defendant corporation, defendant partnership or defendant individual (as the case may be) having been duly served with the application under Rule 3 does not appear on the hearing of the application or, having appeared, fails or refuses to comply with an order made in the proceedings, the Court may make such order as the Court deems appropriate against the contravening person, defendant corporation, defendant partnership or defendant individual, as the case may be.
@ref O 61 r 5(2) (src:7144)
GIVEN `the person was duly served with the application under Rule 3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does not appear on the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person appeared but fails or refuses to comply with an order made in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 5(2) the Court may make such order as it deems appropriate against the contravening person` MEANS
    IF `the person was duly served with the application under Rule 3` AND (`the person does not appear on the hearing` OR `the person appeared but fails or refuses to comply with an order made in the proceedings`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a contravening person, defendant corporation, defendant partnership or defendant individual (as the case may be) having been duly served with the application under Rule 3 does not appear on the hearing of the application or, having appeared, fails or refuses to comply with an order made in the proceedings"

-- src:7145 | (3) Where a claimant having filed an affidavit of claim under Rule 4 does not appear on the hearing of the application or, having appeared, fails or refuses to comply with an order made in the proceedings, the Court may make an order declaring the claimant, and all persons claiming under the claimant, forever barred from bringing any claim against the contravening person, defendant corporation, defendant partnership or defendant individual, as the case may be.
@ref O 61 r 5(3) (src:7145)
GIVEN `the claimant filed an affidavit of claim under Rule 4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant does not appear on the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant appeared but fails or refuses to comply with an order made in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 5(3) the Court may declare the claimant forever barred` MEANS
    IF `the claimant filed an affidavit of claim under Rule 4` AND (`the claimant does not appear on the hearing` OR `the claimant appeared but fails or refuses to comply with an order made in the proceedings`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a claimant having filed an affidavit of claim under Rule 4 does not appear on the hearing of the application or, having appeared, fails or refuses to comply with an order made in the proceedings"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 6 -- other powers`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7147 | 6. Subject to Rules 1 to 5, the Court may, in or for the purposes of any proceedings in this Order, make such order as to costs or any other matter as the Court thinks just.
@ref O 61 r 6 (src:7147)
GIVEN `the order is in or for the purposes of proceedings in this Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of Rules 1 to 5 provides otherwise on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 6 the Court may make such order as to costs or any other matter as it thinks just` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the order is in or for the purposes of proceedings in this Order`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given "in or for the purposes of any proceedings in this Order"
        IF `one of Rules 1 to 5 provides otherwise on the matter`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "Subject to Rules 1 to 5" and where one of them speaks this Rule neither grants nor denies; QA: NOTHING (a displaced grant grants nothing) / other: JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 7 -- trial of issue stated`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7149 | 7. —(1) Order 15 applies, with the necessary modifications, to the trial of an issue stated under Rule 5(1)( c ) as it applies to the trial of an action. (2) The Court by whom an issue stated is tried may give such judgment or make such order as finally to dispose of all questions arising in the proceedings to try the issues stated.
@ref O 61 r 7(1) (src:7149)
GIVEN `the trial is of an issue stated under Rule 5(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 7(1) Order 15 applies to the trial of the issue` MEANS
    IF `the trial is of an issue stated under Rule 5(1)(c)`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- Order 15 applies "with the necessary modifications"; what they are is not in this Order (S-L1: applies with changes, and what changes is NOTHING)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): rule 7(1) speaks of "the trial of an issue stated under Rule 5(1)(c)"

-- src:7149 | 7. —(1) Order 15 applies, with the necessary modifications, to the trial of an issue stated under Rule 5(1)( c ) as it applies to the trial of an action. (2) The Court by whom an issue stated is tried may give such judgment or make such order as finally to dispose of all questions arising in the proceedings to try the issues stated.
@ref O 61 r 7(2) (src:7149)
GIVEN `the Court is the Court by whom an issue stated is tried` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 61 r 7(2) the Court may give such judgment or make such order as finally to dispose of all questions` MEANS
    IF `the Court is the Court by whom an issue stated is tried`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given to "The Court by whom an issue stated is tried"
